# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in real values.
#
#     cp packages/backend/.env.example packages/backend/.env.local

DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/fanboard
THESPORTSDB_API_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Redis. Also a SECURITY CONTROL: rate limiting on POST /players depends on it.
# If Redis is unreachable, both the per-IP and per-venue limits fail open and
# every request is allowed -- logged at error level, but unthrottled. Monitor
# Redis uptime and alert on the fail-open log lines. See RATE_LIMITING.md.
# With auth: redis://user:password@host:6379
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# Optional. Set to "false" to boot the server without background workers
# (integration tests, a one-off container, a read-only replica).
# Read straight from process.env at startup rather than through the validated
# env schema, so a missing THESPORTSDB_API_KEY cannot stop the server booting.
# WORKERS_ENABLED=true

# Optional. One of: debug | info | warn | error | silent. Defaults to info.
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# SECURITY-CRITICAL. Number of reverse proxies that append to X-Forwarded-For
# before the request reaches this app. Defaults to 1.
#
# Rate limiting counts in from the RIGHT of X-Forwarded-For by this many hops,
# because a proxy appends the address it saw and everything to the left is
# caller-supplied.
#
# Get this right for your topology before shipping:
#   direct to the app, no proxy      -> 0
#   one nginx / ALB / Caddy in front -> 1
#   Cloudflare -> nginx -> app       -> 2
#
# Failure modes, measured:
#   too high        -> BYPASS. The read index lands on an entry the attacker
#                      controls, so every request gets a fresh bucket.
#   too low (but>0) -> every client shares the inner proxy's bucket, so the whole
#                      venue collectively gets 5 sessions/hour.
#   0               -> no header trusted, per-IP limiting off, venue ceiling
#                      still applies. Degraded but safe.
#
# Verify by tripping the limit and reading `clientIp` on the rejection log line;
# the success path does not log it. See RATE_LIMITING.md#trusted_proxy_hops.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1

# Cookies are Secure by default. Set to "false" ONLY to serve the patron app
# over plain http on a venue LAN -- a Secure cookie is never sent over http, so
# leaving this at the default there breaks login silently.
# COOKIE_SECURE=true

# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION, and it must be a real process env var, not a value in
# this file. `next start` installs its own SIGTERM handler before the app loads
# and exits the process from it, which cuts off the worker drain. Setting this
# makes Next install nothing and hands shutdown to worker-scheduler.ts.
# NEXT_MANUAL_SIG_HANDLE=1
